  atdPan String
  atdPartyName String [not null]
  atdDeducteeType String
  atdSection String [not null]
  atdRate Decimal [not null]
  atdRateSource String [not null]
  atdBaseAmount Decimal [not null]
  atdTaxAmount Decimal [not null]
  atdVoucherId String
  atdVoucherAccYear String
  atdDocRefno String
  atdDocDate DateTime [not null]
  atdBillId String
  atdBillAccYear String
  atdReversalOfId String
  atdChallanNo String
  atdChallanDate DateTime
  atdChallanBsr String
  atdCertificateNo String
  atdCertificateDate DateTime
  atdRemarks String
  atdIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  atdIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  atdCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  atdCreatedBy String
  atdModifiedOn DateTime
  atdModifiedBy String
  party acc_ledger_master [not null]
  reversalOf acc_tds_register
  reversals acc_tds_register [not null]

  Note: 'The 26Q side. Same shape, same rules, different form — see the header
comment on `AccTcsRegister` above, which covers both.

The one structural difference is `atdDeducteeType`: 26Q reports a company
and a non-company deductee under different codes, and
`acc_ledger_master.led_tds_deductee_type` is where that comes from. TCS has
no equivalent, which is why it is here and not on both.'
}

