  Note: 'sales.promotion_scheme_branch — §2, which branches run the campaign.

Read only when prm_branch_scope = \'LIST\'. prbIsExclude makes "every branch
except two" two rows rather than thirty-eight; an EXCLUDE row always beats
an INCLUDE row for the same branch.

CHECK ck_prb_slno (prb_slno > 0) is enforced in the service, not the DB.

DB-only objects to hand-author in the migration:
ux_prb_row     UNIQUE (prb_prm_id, prb_branch_id) WHERE NOT deleted
ix_prb_scheme  (prb_prm_id) INCLUDE (branch, is_exclude), partial
ix_prb_branch  (prb_branch_id), partial'
}

Table promotion_scheme_item {
  priId String [pk]
  priPrmId String [not null]
  priSlno Int [not null, default: 1]
  priKind String [not null]
  priScopeId String [not null]
  priItemId String
  priGroupId String
  priCategoryId String
  priBrandId String
  priSectionId String
  priUnitId String
  priIsExclude Boolean [not null, default: false]
  priDiscPerc Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  priDiscQty Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  priDiscAmt Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  priMinQty Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  priFactor Decimal [not null, default: 1]
  priMaxBenefit Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  priMatchPriority Int [not null, default: 1]
  priNotes String
  priIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  priIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  priSyncDate DateTime
  priCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  priCreatedBy String
  priModifiedOn DateTime
  priModifiedBy String
  scheme promotion_scheme [not null]
  item item_master
  itemGroup item_group_master
  itemCategory item_category_master
  itemBrand item_brand_master
  itemSection item_section_master
  unit item_unit_conversion

  Note: 'sales.promotion_scheme_item — §4, which stock the campaign applies to.

One kind + one scope id, with five GENERATED ALWAYS ... STORED columns
carrying the foreign keys — the same shape as PromotionSchemeParty, read
that model\'s header for the write rules and the migration caveat. In short:
set priKind + priScopeId (+ priUnitId on an ITEM row) and never touch
itemId / groupId / categoryId / brandId / sectionId.

This is what makes "20% off own-brand, but nothing on tobacco" ONE scheme.

priMatchPriority: most specific wins. Seed ITEM 4, BRAND 3, CATEGORY 2,
SECTION 1, GROUP 0 — data, not a hard-coded rule. An EXCLUDE row kills the
line regardless of any broader rule.

Read only when prm_item_scope = \'LIST\'.

── The discount trio ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
A rate may be stated here, on the item row, instead of on a slab band —
that is all "Discount On Items (Offer Per Item)" ever was. Stored in the
bill\'s own idiom because they are copied straight onto
sbi_sch_disc_perc / _qty / _amt:
priDiscPerc  percentage off the line
priDiscQty   rupees off PER UNIT
priDiscAmt   flat rupees off the line
At most one is non-zero. All three zero = this row only says "in scope".

A unit is REQUIRED on an ITEM row and FORBIDDEN on every other kind:
"10 of item X" is not a quantity until you say ten of WHAT, and a unit is a
row of item_unit_conversion keyed to one item, so on a BRAND or CATEGORY
row it would claim to apply to items that never define it.

CHECK ck_pri_kind, ck_pri_unit, ck_pri_one_rate, ck_pri_exclude,
ck_pri_values, ck_pri_slno and ck_pri_match_priority are enforced in the
service, not the DB.

DB-only objects to hand-author:
ux_pri_row     UNIQUE (prm_id, kind, scope_id) WHERE NOT deleted
ix_pri_scheme  (prm_id, match_priority DESC) INCLUDE (...), partial
ix_pri_item / _group / _category / _brand / _section / _unit, all partial'
}

Table promotion_scheme_party {
  prpId String [pk]
  prpPrmId String [not null]
  prpSlno Int [not null, default: 1]
  prpKind String [not null]
  prpScopeId String [not null]
  prpCustId String
  prpCustGroupId String
  prpAreaId String
  prpCityId String
  prpIsExclude Boolean [not null, default: false]
  prpMatchPriority Int [not null, default: 1]
  prpNotes String
  prpIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  prpIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  prpSyncDate DateTime
  prpCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  prpCreatedBy String
  prpModifiedOn DateTime
  prpModifiedBy String
  scheme promotion_scheme [not null]
  customer customers
  customerGroup cust_groups
  area area_master
  city city_master

  Note: 'sales.promotion_scheme_party — §3, who the campaign applies to.

ONE KIND + ONE SCOPE ID, the shape the entry grid needs. The screen binds
to exactly two columns, prpKind and prpScopeId; the four *_id fields below
are GENERATED ALWAYS ... STORED in Postgres and exist only to carry a real
foreign key per kind.

prpKind = \'CUSTOMER\' | \'CUSTOMER_GROUP\' | \'AREA\' | \'CITY\'

CITY reaches a customer THROUGH THEIR AREA and only that way
(customers.cus_area_id -> area_master.arm_city_id -> city_master.ctm_id);
customers.cus_city is free text and must never be matched on. A customer
with no area is in no city.

prpMatchPriority makes "a rule naming one CUSTOMER beats one naming their
CITY" data rather than an assumption: CUSTOMER 4, AREA 3, CITY 2,
CUSTOMER_GROUP 1 — narrowest first. EXCLUDE beats INCLUDE at equal priority.

Read only when prm_cust_scope = \'LIST\'.

── WRITING THIS MODEL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEVER set custId / custGroupId / areaId / cityId, and never use the four
nested `connect`s. Postgres computes those columns and rejects any write.
Set prpKind + prpScopeId; read the relations back.

── MIGRATION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
prisma migrate cannot emit a generated column. The four must be
hand-authored, e.g.
prp_cust_id uuid GENERATED ALWAYS AS
(CASE WHEN prp_kind::text = \'CUSTOMER\' THEN prp_scope_id END) STORED
The `@default(dbgenerated())` below is the no-argument form: it stops every
later `migrate dev` emitting an ALTER COLUMN ... DROP DEFAULT that Postgres
rejects with 42601 on a generated column.

The FKs are ON UPDATE NO ACTION, not CASCADE — Postgres forbids a cascading
update on a key containing a generated column. Costs nothing: every master
key here is a uuidv7() that is never reissued.

CHECK ck_prp_kind, ck_prp_slno and ck_prp_match_priority are enforced in the
service, not the DB.

DB-only objects to hand-author:
ux_prp_row       UNIQUE (prm_id, kind, scope_id) WHERE NOT deleted
ix_prp_scheme    (prm_id, match_priority DESC) INCLUDE (...), partial
ix_prp_cust / ix_prp_cust_group / ix_prp_area / ix_prp_city, all partial'
}

Table promotion_scheme_slab {
  prsId String [pk]
  prsPrmId String [not null]
  prsSlno Int [not null, default: 1]
  prsBenefit String [not null]
  prsExceeds Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsUpto Decimal
  prsEach Decimal [not null, default: 1]
  prsIsRepeat Boolean [not null, default: false]
  prsMaxRepeats Int [not null, default: 0]
  prsFreeItemId String
  prsFreeUnitId String
  prsFreeQty Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsFreeStockCheck Boolean [not null, default: true]
  prsDiscPerc Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsDiscQty Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsDiscAmt Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsFixedPrice Decimal
  prsMaxBenefitAmt Decimal [not null, default: 0]
  prsNotes String
  prsIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  prsIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  prsSyncDate DateTime
  prsCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  prsCreatedBy String
  prsModifiedOn DateTime
  prsModifiedBy String
  scheme promotion_scheme [not null]
  freeItem item_master
  freeUnit item_unit_conversion

  Note: 'sales.promotion_scheme_slab — §5, the offer bands.

One row = one band. Read as: when the measured value is between prsExceeds
and prsUpto, give the benefit; and if prsIsRepeat, give it once per prsEach
above prsExceeds instead of once in total.

"the measured value" is RUPEES when prm_apply_on is BILL_AMOUNT or
ITEM_AMOUNT, and QUANTITY when it is BILL_QTY or ITEM_QTY — one column pair
serving both, exactly as the loyalty slabs do.

Bands are ROWS, not columns: 0-999 -> 2%, 1000-4999 -> 5%, 5000+ -> 8% is
three rows.

── The benefit is ENFORCED, not merely documented ──────────────────────
prsBenefit is a copy of the header\'s prmBenefit tied to it by a COMPOSITE
foreign key (prs_prm_id, prs_benefit) -> (prm_id, prm_benefit), which is
why PromotionScheme carries the otherwise-redundant
@@unique([prmId, prmBenefit]). A percentage-discount scheme therefore
CANNOT physically hold a free-item band. This composite FK also carries the
ON DELETE CASCADE, so no second plain FK on prsPrmId is declared.

The other half of that pair — ck_prs_benefit_columns, "the benefit column
is filled and the others are empty" — is a CHECK, so it lives in the
service instead of the migration, along with ck_prs_band, ck_prs_each,
ck_prs_amounts, ck_prs_free_unit_pair and ck_prs_slno. The FK still stops
the header and its bands disagreeing; the service is what stops a
DISC_PERC band being saved with a fixed price in it.

DB-only objects to hand-author:
ux_prs_band      UNIQUE (prm_id, exceeds, COALESCE(free_item_id, nil uuid))
WHERE NOT deleted — so "spend 5000, get a mug AND a pen"
is two rows at one threshold, while two rows claiming the
same band with nothing to separate them stays impossible
ix_prs_scheme    (prm_id, benefit, exceeds) INCLUDE (...), partial
ix_prs_free_item / ix_prs_free_unit, partial'
}

